From ed987697f26e48ad087aa46db3090a1aa431056e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: albanread <albanread@googlemail.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 17:28:25 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] prose_display: Haiku's coding style, and nothing else

Includes in the guidelines' groups -- POSIX, the public driver API, then the
private headers -- in ASCII order within each; C++ casts for thirty C ones,
static_cast where the source is void* so those are still checked, and
reinterpret_cast only between unrelated pointer types or for the event index
the virtqueue carries in its void* tag; three lines brought within 100 columns,
two of whose statements then span lines and so take braces; the trailing
comment on PRDS_TEST_PATTERN moved above it; and a doc comment in the form the
rest of the file uses.

No change in behaviour. PRDS_TEST_PATTERN stays: it is a documented switch for
the driver's self-test, turned off in patch 0034, not code left behind. Two of
the casts are inside it and so are not compiled while it is off; they were
converted by reading their types, not by the compiler.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Prose-Patch: 0126-prose-display-haiku-s-coding-style-and-nothing-else.patch 4c0b369dad682f933cd64c1feed9058d3d4492099ba364fa44fe999012ddffca
